# The UNCOVERED ceiling. check-ledger.sh fails if the ledger's UNCOVERED count RISES above it.
#
# Why a checked-in number and not just a printed one: a printed count is something you can
# stop reading. This one has to be edited by hand, in a commit, which makes progress and
# regression both visible in the diff — and makes "the corpus quietly shrank" impossible,
# because deleting a test raises the count and breaks the build.
#
# LOWER it whenever coverage lands.
#
# RAISE it only when the count rose because hidden work became VISIBLE — a section moving out
# of N/A into UNCOVERED. Never to accommodate a test that was deleted, a marker that was
# dropped, or a section reclassified out of COVERED: those mean coverage was LOST, and each
# wants explaining rather than absorbing. The distinction is the whole point, so a raise
# carries its reason here.
#
# 443 -> 441 (this commit): §3.8 and §3.9 covered by conformance/jls/Ch3.java — the first
# lowering, and the direction this number is supposed to move.
#
# 427 -> 443 (previous): sixteen §13 sections were marked N/A on the premise that javelina
# does a "whole-program compile" with no pre-existing binaries. That premise is FALSE:
# `javelinac --mode jre` builds jre.wasm and a plugin IMPORTS from that module, so a plugin
# compiled against one jre and run against a changed one IS §13's scenario — and the project
# already carries an unfixed bug in exactly that seam (a library import changing a descriptor).
# On this target the break surfaces as a link/validation failure rather than the class-file
# error the section names, which is a difference in FORM, not in observability.
#
# 422 -> 427 (previous): five §20/§22 sections were marked N/A with reasons that described
# what had been WRITTEN rather than what is OBSERVABLE — "No Runtime.java", "exists but is a
# 5-line empty placeholder", "not part of the implemented runtime". java.io.StreamTokenizer is
# pure Java needing no thread and no host capability; it is unwritten, not inapplicable. An N/A
# row is invisible to this ratchet forever, so that was a permanent hiding place. ClassLoader,
# Process, Runtime, SecurityManager and StreamTokenizer are now UNCOVERED, which is what
# unwritten means, and check-ledger.sh now rejects an N/A justified by implementation state.
441
